From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] main: read the UAPI system config hierarchy
Source: Nex
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

get_config_path only tries SYSCONFDIR "/swayidle/config" after the user
files, so a package cannot ship a default under /usr/lib and a boot-time
tool has nowhere under /run to place a temporary override.

Walk the same three tiers other Nex-patched readers use after the user
files: SYSCONFDIR (the administrator's /etc), then /run, then /usr/lib.
Keep the existing user paths and their priority, and keep the -C override
untouched.

diff -urN a/main.c b/main.c
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -975,10 +975,12 @@
 }

 static char *get_config_path(void) {
-	static char *config_paths[3] = {
+	static char *config_paths[5] = {
 		"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/swayidle/config",
 		"$HOME/.swayidle/config",
 		SYSCONFDIR "/swayidle/config",
+		"/run/swayidle/config",
+		"/usr/lib/swayidle/config",
 	};

 	char *config_home = getenv("XDG_CONFIG_HOME");
